  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### Added\n- **Telegram Business support.** Three attributes route the business update types: `[BusinessMessage]` (`business_message`, plus `edited_business_message` with `IncludeEdited = true`), `[BusinessConnection]` (`business_connection`, optionally narrowed to `BusinessConnectionEvent.Connected` / `Disconnected`), and `[BusinessMessagesDeleted]` (`deleted_business_messages`). `[BusinessMessage]` takes the same `Pattern` / `Contains` / `Regex` / `State` filters as `[Text]`, and defaults to `From = BusinessSender.Customer` so a bot never reacts to what the account owner types (`BusinessSender.Owner` / `Any` opt into the other side).\n- `Context.BusinessConnectionId` and `Context.IsBusiness`, plus `Context.Business` (`Connection`, `ConnectionId`, `Message`, `DeletedMessages`, `Rights`, `CanReply`, `IsEnabled`, `FromOwner`) for the business view of an update.\n- `BusinessConnection` and `BusinessMessagesDeleted` bind directly as handler parameters, like `Message` and `ChatMemberUpdated` already did.\n- `TestBot` can drive business chats: `SendBusinessConnection`, `SendBusinessMessage`, `SendBusinessMessageFromOwner`, `SendBusinessMessagesDeleted`.\n\n### Changed\n- `Context.Reply` now sends with the update's `business_connection_id`, so replies in a business chat are posted on behalf of the business account. Ordinary chats are unaffected (the id is `null`).\n- `Context.ChatId` resolves business updates: the customer's chat for messages and deletions, the owner's `UserChatId` for connection updates.\n- Kippo's allowed-updates list now includes `business_connection`, `business_message`, `edited_business_message` and `deleted_business_messages`, and webhook mode passes that list to `SetWebhook` (previously it relied on Telegram's default, which omits `chat_member`). Both transports now subscribe to the same set.\n- `Message` / `Contact` handler parameters and `Context.Message.Text` / `.Contact` also resolve business (and edited) messages instead of only `Update.Message`.",
